# InteliBoy - the packages added on top of the core.
#
# The appliance runs one program. This list is the runtime closure of avatari
# and grub, computed with 'make closure PACKAGES="x-make-avatari 5-make-grub"'
# and put back into build order, plus two things no dependency graph can see:
#
#   ca certificates   nothing in the image had any, so every HTTPS request
#                     failed CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED — the model adapter and
#                     the http tool alike. p11-kit, make-ca and the trust store
#                     itself, plus libtasn1 which p11-kit needs
#   python            cogiti and audi are both python. Its closure adds gdbm,
#                     libffi and sqlite, computed with
#                     'make closure PACKAGES=8.51-make-python' and diffed
#                     against core — 21 of its 25 dependencies were already
#                     here for other reasons
#   the kernel        every distro names its own now, see distros/core
#   alsa-utils        alsactl unmutes the mixer at boot; nothing links it
#   dejavu fonts      avatari opens the face by path from /etc/avatari.conf,
#                     so nothing links it and 'make check' cannot miss it
#                     either - it simply has no way to know
#
# Worth knowing what is in here and why it looks wrong: the X client libraries
# (libX11, libxcb, libXau, libXdmcp) and the font stack (fontconfig, freetype,
# harfbuzz) are pulled in by Mesa, not by avatari. Our Mesa is the desktop one,
# built -Dplatforms=x11 -Dglx=dri, so libGL links the X libraries even though
# there is no X server here to talk to. A Mesa built -Dplatforms= would drop
# every one of them. That is the first thing to trim once this boots.
#
# gcc is here for libstdc++ and libgcc_s, which Mesa needs and which LFS ships
# as part of the compiler package. It is not here so the appliance can compile.
#
# Lines starting with # and empty lines are ignored, the order is the order the
# packages are installed in.

